{
  "week": 3,
  "title": "Data Access and Management",
  "topicSummary": "SQL, APIs, web scraping, data cleaning, cloud storage.",
  "content": [
    {
      "type": "section_heading",
      "text": "1. Overview"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "After learning what data is (Week 2), this module focuses on how to access, retrieve, process, and store urban data efficiently."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "<strong>Core Pipeline:</strong> Data Sources → Access (SQL/APIs/Scraping) → Cleaning → Storage (Cloud)"
    },
    {
      "type": "section_heading",
      "text": "2. SQL (Structured Query Language)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "<strong>Definition:</strong> SQL is used to query and manipulate data stored in relational databases."
    },
    {
      "type": "sub_heading",
      "text": "Core Operations:"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "headers": [
        "Operation",
        "Purpose",
        "Example"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "SELECT",
          "Retrieve data",
          "Get traffic records"
        ],
        [
          "INSERT",
          "Add data",
          "Add new sensor data"
        ],
        [
          "UPDATE",
          "Modify data",
          "Update vehicle speed"
        ],
        [
          "DELETE",
          "Remove data",
          "Delete incorrect entries"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "sql",
      "code": "-- Example Query\nSELECT location, AVG(speed)\nFROM traffic_data\nWHERE time = '08:00'\nGROUP BY location;"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "👉 This calculates average speed per location at a specific time."
    },
    {
      "type": "sub_heading",
      "text": "Key Concepts:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Filtering → <strong>WHERE</strong>",
        "Aggregation → <strong>AVG(), COUNT()</strong>",
        "Grouping → <strong>GROUP BY</strong>",
        "Joining tables → <strong>JOIN</strong>"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "sub_heading",
      "text": "Use in Urban Informatics:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Traffic analysis",
        "Population statistics",
        "Infrastructure monitoring"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "section_heading",
      "text": "3. APIs (Application Programming Interfaces)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "<strong>Definition:</strong> APIs allow systems to communicate and exchange data programmatically."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "👉 Instead of manually downloading data, you request it via API."
    },
    {
      "type": "sub_heading",
      "text": "How APIs Work:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "ordered",
      "items": [
        "Client sends request",
        "Server processes request",
        "Server returns data (usually JSON)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "sub_heading",
      "text": "Example (Conceptual):"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "import requests\nresponse = requests.get(\"https://api.weather.com/data\")\ndata = response.json()"
    },
    {
      "type": "sub_heading",
      "text": "Types of APIs:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "REST APIs (most common)",
        "SOAP APIs (older, structured)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "sub_heading",
      "text": "Urban Use Cases:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Weather data APIs",
        "Traffic updates",
        "Public transport schedules"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "section_heading",
      "text": "4. Web Scraping"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "<strong>Definition:</strong> Web scraping is the process of extracting data from websites automatically."
    },
    {
      "type": "sub_heading",
      "text": "When to Use:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "No API available",
        "Data is publicly displayed on websites"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "sub_heading",
      "text": "Tools:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Python libraries: BeautifulSoup, Scrapy, Selenium."
    },
    {
      "type": "sub_heading",
      "text": "Example (Conceptual):"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "from bs4 import BeautifulSoup\nimport requests\nhtml = requests.get(\"https://example.com\").text\nsoup = BeautifulSoup(html, \"html.parser\")\ndata = soup.find_all(\"table\")"
    },
    {
      "type": "sub_heading",
      "text": "Caution:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Legal restrictions (respect robots.txt)",
        "Ethical considerations",
        "Website structure may change"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "section_heading",
      "text": "5. Data Cleaning"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "<strong>Definition:</strong> Data cleaning is the process of preparing raw data for analysis."
    },
    {
      "type": "sub_heading",
      "text": "Common Issues:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Missing values",
        "Duplicate records",
        "Inconsistent formats",
        "Outliers"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "sub_heading",
      "text": "Techniques:"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "headers": [
        "Problem",
        "Solution"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Missing values",
          "Fill (mean/median) or remove"
        ],
        [
          "Duplicates",
          "Drop duplicates"
        ],
        [
          "Inconsistent format",
          "Standardize"
        ],
        [
          "Noise/outliers",
          "Filter or smooth"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "sub_heading",
      "text": "Example (Python - Pandas):"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "import pandas as pd\ndf = pd.read_csv(\"traffic.csv\")\ndf = df.drop_duplicates()\ndf = df.fillna(df.mean())"
    },
    {
      "type": "sub_heading",
      "text": "Importance:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Improves model accuracy",
        "Ensures reliable analysis",
        "Reduces errors"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "section_heading",
